{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYFxs1pQZa7Tz4rgftb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wikimedia's brief in the OpenAI copyright litigation spells out what it would accept for the content it hosts. Uncredited use should be limited to model training. Any use for retrieval-augmented generation, or newer techniques that serve a similar grounding purpose, must give proper attribution under Wikipedia's Creative Commons CC BY-SA 4.0 license. That license requires credit to the original creators and requires remixes or adaptations to stay under the same license. Wikimedia adds that scraping of its projects must follow its public API rate limits or go through its Enterprise API offerings, whatever the use case.\n\nThe terms come from an organization whose content is already inside these systems. Wikipedia has more than 67 million articles in 300 languages, and the article describes it as one of the highest-quality datasets used to train LLMs and a source behind chatbots, search engines and voice assistants. Wikimedia's position gives up attribution for training, provided the resulting model is something new and different from its sources, and asks for it when a chatbot retrieves and delivers existing content.\n\nGeneral Counsel Stephen LaPorte argues that the fair use conversation cannot be limited to for-profit organizations and must include stakeholders across the online information ecosystem. The case itself is between The New York Times and OpenAI and Microsoft, and an amicus brief is an opinion offered to the court. The article does not say how the court will weigh it, and no ruling has been issued. What the filing does establish is that a nonprofit running one of the web's most widely used reference sites wants the court to treat training and retrieval as separate questions."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1333,"cache_read_input_tokens":3339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1333},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cf95dce-9255-429f-a813-98c096d73638","uuid":"78ca28c3-9147-4313-b195-1de44cc845b5","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:21:19.454Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYFxf7qNcSkjFvxAmrP"}
